prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Clarion County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 32 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 47% of normal in July to August and 55% in August to September. June to July is the wettest pair at 9.12 inches normal, and January to February is the driest at 5.72 inches. Grid 25102 had its driest year in 1991 at 68% of normal.</p>"}
